{"name":"Night Music","hex":"#9c96af","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"},{"term":"music","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A series of sounds organized in time, usually employing some combination of harmony, melody, rhythm, tempo, timbre, sound design, lyrics, etc., often to convey a mood.","Any interesting or pleasing sounds."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To seduce or entice with music."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/music"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night Music (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Music is a 1940 play by Clifford Odets. Written in 1939 and produced by the Group Theatre, the play was a commercial failure, closing after 20 performances."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Music_(play)","wikidata":"Q16885607"},{"title":"A Little Night Music","blocks":[{"text":"A Little Night Music is a musical with music and lyrics by Stephen Sondheim and book by Hugh Wheeler. Inspired by the 1955 Ingmar Bergman film Smiles of a Summer Night, it involves the romantic lives of several couples. Its title is a literal English translation of the German name for Mozart's Serenade No. 13, K. 525, Eine kleine Nachtmusik. The musical includes the popular song \"Send In the Clowns\", written for Glynis Johns."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/A_Little_Night_Music_%28theatrical_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Little_Night_Music","wikidata":"Q2530921"},{"title":"Night Music (Joe Jackson album)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Music is the 12th studio album by Joe Jackson, released in 1994 on Virgin Records. The album did not chart. Soon after the album's release, Jackson moved to the Sony Classical label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/JoeJacksonNightMusic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Music_(Joe_Jackson_album)","wikidata":"Q7033373"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/A_Little_Night_Music_%28theatrical_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/A_Little_Night_Music_%28theatrical_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APnight.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7d/A_Little_Night_Music_%281995_cast_recording_-_cover_art%29.jpg/250px-A_Little_Night_Music_%281995_cast_recording_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/